  "methods": [
    "The first seven calendar days from the earliest common archive date were fixed before examining response results. Actual collector timestamps define inclusion; partition date labels are not assumed to be UTC.",
    "A spot shock is a Binance recorded trade-price log change of at least 5 basis points over the preceding 1 second (lookback observation at most 250 ms older). The 2- and 10-basis-point floors are declared sensitivities. Keep the earliest candidate and then wait 10 seconds before selecting another, without inspecting future quotes.",
    "Match only the UP side of the active BTC 15-minute contract; nominal start/end are encoded by its archive slug. Require at least 30 seconds before nominal end and an initial midpoint between 5% and 95%.",
    "Use (best bid + best ask)/2, not the price-change payload price. At every sampled time require 0 < bid <= ask < 1, spread <=10 percentage points, and a latest quote no more than 1 second old. Invalid quotes reset availability rather than being silently skipped.",
    "The baseline is the last valid recorded midpoint strictly before the spot threshold crossing. A response means its signed change first reaches +1 percentage point by 5 seconds. Crossing fractions count all complete eligible paths; median delay is conditional on responding and separately labeled.",
    "Follow-up grid is 0, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000 and 5000 ms. Missing/stale paths are excluded and counted. No interpolation or zero-movement imputation.",
    "The opposite-direction diagnostic uses the same episodes and records whether the midpoint ever moves at least 1 point against the spot shock; both directions can be reached within the same window. It is descriptive, not a randomized placebo.",
    "No statistical interval is presented from this short, incomplete historical cohort. Day-by-day results expose variation; episodes and adjacent contracts share Bitcoin information."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Collector-clock delays combine exchange reaction, feed transport and collection latency. They are not end-to-end trader reaction times.",
    "Spot threshold crossing occurs after a move has begun; Polymarket can already have reacted before the chosen zero. First quote response does not mean full information absorption.",
    "Complete fresh-price paths select active observed periods. Archive gaps and the tiny February 13 recording limit representativeness.",
    "A spot-price move is a continuous information proxy, not an independently identified news announcement. Further spot movement can drive the follow-up.",
    "The actual downloaded market_meta table has no authoritative resolved-outcome field despite the README reference schema. We do not infer outcomes from prices; forecast calibration or added predictive value versus spot is not established by this audit.",
    "This is a new descriptive calculation on one fixed week, not a reproduction of the paper\u2019s published 347 ms figure, and no execution/fee or profitability claim is made."
  ],
